Are we so sure {stanruasabi} isn't a type-3 fu'ivla? The fu'ivla types are=
=20
just a convention anyway. I know the Book says the "tail" of a type-3=20
fu'ivla should start with a consonant, but a glide {ua} is _nearly_ a=20
consonant. Furthermore, syllable analysis (using camxes) gives us=20
{sta,nr,ua,sa,bi} which has that telltale consonantal syllable.

So I say {stanruasabi} is type-3 and fine. What do you think?

mu'o mi'e la durkavore

